                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The Psychiatric Technician (PT) provides general behavioral training and psychiatric nursing care to STAR residents. &nbsp;</span><a name="_Hlk79501684"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The PT will perform on-site direct care and training with consumers. &nbsp;The PT will provide cross-training to the consumer’s community home staff or family.</span></a><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> &nbsp;Will maintain credentials in required Psychiatric Technician and required trainings. The PT may actively participate as part of the Inter-Disciplinary Team (IDT) at monthly IPPs, restraint debriefings, and other meetings for the consumer. &nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span><span> </span></span></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span>&nbsp;</span></span></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=23102598&name=DS-PTSTAR2.2024.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
